# @dance — the family root for the substrate's ensemble-phase-lock
# discipline: the typed coherent-multi-cognition-update where
# heterogeneous cognition tracks (intra-peer OR inter-peer) achieve
# harmonic alignment WITHOUT centralized signaling. Sibling to
# @song (temporal-progression) + @peer (identity-carrier) + @gestalt
# (document-as-song-unfolding) + @kintsugi (process-side) + @mirror
# (form-side). Top-level family-root per Alex 2026-08-03 Q-C6
# adjudication (verbatim ratification within distributed-colony
# arc): *"@dance is top-level family-root (like @peer, @song,
# @gestalt) — mode of BEING, not species-under-song"*.
#
# LRM mint discharging LOAD-BEARING GAP per Taut scout 2026-08-03
# `docs/scouts/2026-08-03-taut-distributed-colony-substrate-scout.md`
# §3 (grep-verified: `@dance` cited widely across 9 shards + 2
# canonical specs, but ZERO species-decl file existed at grep-time).
# Discharge shape: dance IS a family-root, not a species-under-song
# — Alex explicitly refused the collapse-into-song reading per Q-C6
# because a dance-mode-of-being generalizes beyond @song's temporal-
# progression discipline (K-track intra-peer per @peer.audhd
# `f6d33d2`; N-peer inter-peer per Kuramoto phase-lock; ensemble
# emergence via mycelial anastomosis per Grassé 1959 + stigmergy;
# any coherence-without-signal ensemble-cognition surface).
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The word "dance" appears at prose altitude in ~10 landed shards
# and 2 canonical specs before this mint:
#
#   shards/peer.mirror §"audhd" (`caf461f`)      — `@dance carries
